  "summary": "Optimizes BIP352 silent payment input key extraction for P2SH inputs by checking the witness stack before evaluating the scriptSig. Because only P2SH-P2WPKH inputs are eligible and consensus requires non-segwit P2SH inputs to have an empty witness, inputs without a compressed witness public key are rejected immediately.",
  "problem": "When scanning transactions for silent payment eligibility, verifying whether a P2SH input is P2SH-P2WPKH evaluates the scriptSig before checking for a witness. Non-segwit P2SH inputs can carry scriptSigs up to 10,000 bytes, causing unnecessary script evaluation overhead during block or transaction scanning.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit message and PR description: \"Consensus forbids a witness on non-segwit P2SH inputs, so check the witness (and the cheap pubkey size check) before evaluating the scriptSig. This avoids evaluating scriptSigs of up to MAX_SCRIPT_SIZE for the common case of non-segwit P2SH spends.\""
